hat <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;contains exactly <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn></math> balls is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>k</mi><msup><mfenced><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mn>9</mn></msup></math> then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>k</mi></math> lies in the set :"}, "options": [{"id": "d877de", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>{</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>:</mo><mo>|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>|</mo><mo>&#60;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>}</mo></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2c2ee0e063d924929b"}, {"id": "6612d3", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>{</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>:</mo><mo>|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>|</mo><mo>&#8804;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>}</mo></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2c2ee0e063d924929c"}, {"id": "2e5cfe", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>{</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>:</mo><mo>|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>|</mo><mo>&#60;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>}</mo></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2c2ee0e063d924929d"}, {"id": "d52bd4", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>{</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>:</mo><mo>|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>|</mo><mo>&#8804;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>}</mo></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2c2ee0e063d924929e"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f2c2ee0e063d924929f", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df9c"], "topics": ["60e2fb3c66f9ce3f243b4d5a"], "concepts": ["6117b03dc5f0702080bdea7d"], "question": {"text": "Let M be the maximum value of the product of two positive integers when their sum is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>66</mn></math>&nbsp;. Let the sample space <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>S</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"}\" open=\"{\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo>:</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>(</mo><mn>66</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>&#8805;</mo><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mn>9</mn></mfrac><mi>M</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> and the event <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>{</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mo>:</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></math> is a multiple of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn></math>}. Then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>)</mo></math> is equal to"}, "options": [{"id": "ae9b54", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>15</mn><mn>44</mn></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2c2ee0e063d92492a0"}, {"id": "361066", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2c2ee0e063d92492a1"}, {"id": "5848c5", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2c2ee0e063d92492a2"}, {"id": "1e916d", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>7</mn><mn>22</mn></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2c2ee0e063d92492a3"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f2c2ee0e063d92492a4", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df9c"], "topics": ["60e2fb3c66f9ce3f243b4d5a"], "concepts": ["60e2fb3c66f9ce3f243b4d2a"], "question": {"text": "If <math><mn>10</mn></math> different balls are to be placed in <math><mn>4</mn></math> distinct boxes at random, then the probability that two of these boxes contain exactly <math><mn>2</mn></math> and <math><mn>3</mn></math> balls is:"}, "opti