"682283", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>16</mn></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2c2ee0e063d92492b6"}, {"id": "6162af", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2c2ee0e063d92492b7"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f2c2ee0e063d92492b8", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df9c"], "topics": ["60e2fb3c66f9ce3f243b4d5a"], "concepts": ["60e2fb3c66f9ce3f243b4d2a"], "question": {"text": "A coin is biased so that a head is twice as likely to occur as a tail. If the coin is tossed <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn></math> times, then the probability of getting two tails and one head is-"}, "options": [{"id": "a7d06e", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>9</mn></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2c2ee0e063d92492b9"}, {"id": "5fb49b", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>9</mn></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2c2ee0e063d92492ba"}, {"id": "b49e1b", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>27</mn></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2c2ee0e063d92492bb"}, {"id": "7033c7", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>27</mn></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2c2ee0e063d92492bc"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f2c2ee0e063d92492bd", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df9c"], "topics": ["60e2fb3c66f9ce3f243b4d5a"], "concepts": ["60e2fb3c66f9ce3f243b4d2a"], "question": {"text": "<p>In a random experiment, a fair die is rolled until two fours are obtained in succession. The probability that the experiment will end in the fifth throw of the die is equal to :</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "c81bd8", "text": "<math><mfrac><mrow><mn>150</mn></mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mn>6</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2c2ee0e063d92492be"}, {"id": "e2d923", "text": "<math><mfrac><mrow><mn>175</mn></mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mn>6</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2c2ee0e063d92492bf"}, {"id": "b41801", "text": "<math><mfrac><mrow><mn>225</mn></mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mn>6</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2c2ee0e063d92492c0"}, {"id": "9394df", "text": "<math><mfrac><mrow><mn>200</mn></mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mn>6</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2c2ee0e063d92492c1"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f2c2ee0e063d92492c2", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df9c"], "topics": ["60e2fb3c66f9ce3f243b4d5a"], "concepts": ["60e2fb3c66f9ce3f243b4d2a"], "question": {"text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>N</mi></math> denote the sum of the numbers obtained when two dice are rolled. If the probability that&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>N</mi></msup><mo>&#60;</mo><mi>N</mi><mo>!</mo></math>&nbsp;is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>m</mi><mi>n</mi></mfrac></math>&nbsp;where&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi></math>&nbsp;are coprime, then&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mi>m</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>n</mi></math>&nbsp;is equal to&nbsp;"}, "options": [{"id": "67e489", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2c2ee0e063d92492c3"}, {"id": "f19cf1", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>12</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2c2ee0e063d92492c4"}, {"id": "0e4512", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2c2ee0e063d92492c5"}, {"id": "5a8896", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>8</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2c2ee0e063d92492c6"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f2c2ee0e063d92492c7", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df9c"], "topics": ["60e2fb3c66f9ce3f243b4d5a"], "concepts": ["60e2fb3c66f9ce3f243b4d2a"], "question": {"text": "One die has two faces marked 1 , two faces marked 2 , one face marked 3 and one face marked 4 . Another die has one face marked 1 , two faces marked 2 , two faces marked 3 and one face marked 4. The probability of getting the sum of numbers to be 4 or 5 , when both the dice are thrown together, is"}, "options": [{"id": "08b6fa", "text": "$\\frac{2}{3}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2c2ee0e063d92492c8"}, {"id": "828b35", "text": "$\\frac{1}{2}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2c2ee0e063d92492c9"}, {"id": "c4df1a", "text": "$\\frac{4}{9}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2c2ee0e063d92492ca"}, {"id": "e1d963", "text": "$\\frac{3}{5}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2c2ee0e063d92492cb"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f2c2ee0e063d92492cc", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df9c"], "topics": ["60e2fb3c66f9ce3f243b4d5a"], "concepts": ["60e2fb3c66f9ce3f243b4d2a"], "question": {"text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>S</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>}</mo><mo>.</mo></math>&nbsp;Then the probability that a randomly chosen onto function <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>g</mi></math> from <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>S</mi></math> to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>S</mi></math> satisfies <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>g</mi><mfenced><mn>3</mn></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>g</mi><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced></math> is :"}, "options": [{"id": "8001a1", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>15</mn></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2c2ee0e063d92492cd"}, {"id": "f0db31", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2c2ee0e063d92492ce"}, {"id": "005cec", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>30</mn></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2c2ee0e063d92492cf"}, {"id": "fe74e3", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>10</mn></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2c2ee0e063d92492d0"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f2c2ee0e063d92492d1", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df9c"], "topics": ["60e2fb3c66f9ce3f243b4d5a"], "concepts": ["60e2fb3c66f9ce3f243b4d2a"], "question": {"text": "Five numbers <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>5</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;are randomly selected from the numbers<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#8230;</mo><mo>&#8230;</mo><mo>,</mo><mn>18</mn></math> &nbsp;and are arranged in the increasing order <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&#60;</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#60;</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&#60;</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>&#60;</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced></math>. The probability that <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>7</mn></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>11</mn></math>&nbsp;is"}, "options": [{"id": "ef3ee5", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>136</mn></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2c2ee0e063d92492d2"}, {"id": "7c9ea9", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>68</mn></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2c2ee0e063d92492d3"}, {"id": "a0a9e5", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>7</mn><mn>68</mn></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2c2ee0e063d92492d4"}, {"id": "bea379", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mn>68</mn></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2c2ee0e063d92492d5"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f2c2ee0e063d92492d6", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df9c"], "topics": ["60e2fb3c66f9ce3f243b4d5a"], "concepts": ["60e2fb3c66f9ce3f243b4d2a"], "question": {"text": "If three letters can be posted to any one of the 5 different addresses, then the probability that the three letters are posted to exactly two addresses is:"}, "options": [{"id": "dc9da5", "text": "$\\frac{18}{25}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2c2ee0e063d92492d7"}, {"id": "58d0f8", "text": "$\\frac{12}{25}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2c2ee0e063d92492d8"}, {"id": "196133", "text": "$\\frac{6}{25}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2c2ee0e063d92492d9"}, {"id": "5b7d86", "text": "$\\frac{4}{25}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2c2ee0e063d92492da"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f2c2ee0e063d92492db", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df9c"], "topics": ["60e2fb3c66f9ce3f243b4d5a"], "concepts": ["60e2fb3c66f9ce3f243b4d2a"], "question": {"text": "<p>Three dice are rolled. If the probability of getting different numbers on the three dice is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>p</mi><mi>q</mi></mfrac><mo>,</mo></math>&nbsp;where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>p</mi></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>q</mi></math>&nbsp;are co-prime, then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>q</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>p</mi></math>&nbsp;is equal to</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "3193ba", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2c2ee0e063d92492dc"}, {"id": "7c5e3d", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2c2ee0e063d92492dd"}, {"id": "814792", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2c2ee0e063d92492de"}, {"id": "320d5a", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2c2ee0e063d92492df"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f2c2ee0e063d92492e0", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df9c"], "topics": ["60e2fb3c66f9ce3f243b4d5a"], "concepts": ["60e2fb3c66f9ce3f243b4d2a"], "question": {"text": "Two number $\\mathrm{k}_1$ and $\\mathrm{k}_2$ are randomly chosen from the set of natural numbers. Then, the probability that the value of $\\mathrm{i}^{\\mathrm{k}_1}+\\mathrm{i}^{\\mathrm{k}_2},(\\mathrm{i}=\\sqrt{-1})$ is non-zero, equals"}, "options": [{"id": "f00ab3", "text": "$\\frac{1}{2}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2c2ee0e063d92492e1"}, {"id": "2205da", "text": "$\\frac{3}{4}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2c2ee0e063d92492e2"}, {"id": "914f5d", "text": "$\\frac{1}{4}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2c2ee0e063d92492e3"}, {"id": "654676", "text": "$\\frac{2}{3}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2c2ee0e063d92492e4"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f2c2ee0e063d92492e5", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df9c"], "topics": ["60e2fb3c66f9ce3f243b4d5a"], "concepts": ["60e2fb3c66f9ce3f243b4d2a"], "question": {"text": "<p>Two squares are chosen at random on a chessboard (see figure). The probability that they have a side in common is :</p><p><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2Ff24da50c-1bca-49e3-8233-876270f8b013-image.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 355px; height: 218px;\" /></p>"}, "options": [{"id": "967909", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>9</mn></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2c2ee0e063d92492e6"}, {"id": "c17601", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>7</mn></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2c2ee0e063d92492e7"}, {"id": "94486c", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>7</mn></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2c2ee0e063d92492e8"}, {"id": "bbec36", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>18</mn></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2c2ee0e063d92492e9"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f2c2ee0e063d92492ea", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df9c"], "topics": ["60e2fb3c66f9ce3f243b4d5a"], "concepts": ["60e2fb3c66f9ce3f243b4d2a"], "question": {"text": "Out of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>60</mn><mo>%</mo></math> female and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>40</mn><mo>%</mo></math> male candidates appearing in an exam, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>60</mn><mo>%</mo></math> candidates qualify it. The number of females qualifying the exam is twice the number of males qualifying it. A candidate is randomly chosen from the qualified candidates. The probability, that the chosen candidate is a female, is"}, "options": [{"id": "277682", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2c2ee0e063d92492eb"}, {"id": "2e82df", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>11</mn><mn>16</mn></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2c2ee0e063d92492ec"}, {"id": "0c08d7", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>23</mn><mn>32</mn></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2c2ee0e063d92492ed"}, {"id": "18290e", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>13</mn><mn>16</mn></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2c2ee0e063d92492ee"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f2c2ee0e063d92492ef", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df9c"], "topics": ["60e2fb3c66f9ce3f243b4d5a"], "concepts": ["60e2fb3c66f9ce3f243b4d2a"], "question": {"text": "A bag contains <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn></math> white and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn></math> black balls. A die is rolled once and the number of balls equal to the number obtained on the die are drawn from the bag at random. The probability that all the balls drawn are white is"}, "options": [{"id": "3f6296", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2c2ee0e063d92492f0"}, {"id": "5ab999", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>11</mn><mn>50</mn></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2c2ee0e063d92492f1"}, {"id": "ec280a", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2c2ee0e063d92492f2"}, {"id": "340c9b", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>9</mn><mn>50</mn></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2c2ee0e063d92492f3"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f2c2ee0e063d92492f4", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df9c"], "topics": ["60e2fb3c66f9ce3f243b4d5a"], "concepts": ["60e2fb3c66f9ce3f243b4d2a"], "question": {"text": "Let S be the set of all the words that can be formed by arranging all the letters of the word GARDEN. From the set S, one word is selected at random. The probability that the selected word will NOT have vowels in alphabetical order is :"}, "options": [{"id": "a0cf11", "text": "$\\frac{1}{2}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2c2ee0e063d92492f5"}, {"id": "64031a", "text": "$\\frac{1}{4}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2c2ee0e063d92492f6"}, {"id": "ce07cc", "text": "$\\frac{2}{3}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2c2ee0e063d92492f7"}, {"id": "41e5f4", "text": "$\\frac{1}{3}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2c2ee0e063d92492f8"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f2c2ee0e063d92492f9", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df9c"], "topics": ["60e2fb3c66f9ce3f243b4d5a"], "concepts": ["60e2fb3c66f9ce3f243b4d2a"], "question": {"text": "Four dice are thrown simultaneously and the numbers shown on these dice are recorded in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>2</mn></math>&nbsp;matrices. The probability that such formed matrices have all different entries and are non-singular, is:"}, "options": [{"id": "f8af45", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>45</mn><mn>162</mn></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2c2ee0e063d92492fa"}, {"id": "34d0c6", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>23</mn><mn>81</mn></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2c2ee0e063d92492fb"}, {"id": "6e2da4", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>22</mn><mn>81</mn></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2c2ee0e063d92492fc"}, {"id": "69e097", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>43</mn><mn>162</mn></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2c2ee0e063d92492fd"}], "questionLabels": []}], "markingScheme": {"_id": "608283e223cf4b3ad8f125e6", "title": "JEE Single Correct", "correctAttempt": 4, "incorrectAttempt": -1, "createdAt": "2021-04-09T08:45:27.797Z", "updatedAt": "2021-07-05T05:39:15.785Z", "__v": 0, "updated_by": "6042252509c5bf34e8a2f178"}, "maximumAttemptLimit": 25, "linkedQuestions": [], "createdAt": "2026-04-14T14:29:00.718Z", "updatedAt": "2026-04-14T14:29:00.718Z", "__v": 0}, "position": 0, "_id": "69de4f2c2ee0e063d9249305"}], "bonusSections": [], "packDetails": [], "paidFeatures": [], "tags": [], "timeRestrictionSlots": [], "createdAt": "2026-04-14T11:16:13.786Z", "updatedAt": "2026-04-17T04:58:07.040Z", "testType": "PYQs as Chapter Tests", "isResumeBufferAllowed": true, "enableAccessibility": true, "maxAttemptableQuestion": 25, "analysisVideoThumbnail": "", "analysisVideoThumbnailDark": "", "shortTitle": "", "subjectDetails": [{"subjectId": "607018ee404ae53194e73d92", "title": "Mathematics", "shortName": "Math"}], "testTimerType": "mm", "isMarkForReviewAvailable": true}, "temporaryTestDetail": {"_id": "6a4a1f1f9cbf3c651306d0aa", "testId": "69de21fd7e39d99b57bc5bd5", "userId": "6914cc9c4d7566258ee3a8fd", "startedAt": "2026-07-05T09:08:47.174Z", "lastAttemptedSection": null, "totalTimeLeft": 75, "bonusAttempt": false, "sections": [{"sectionId": "69de4f2c2ee0e063d9249303", "questions": [{"questionId": "69de4f2c2ee0e063d9249281", "markedOptions": [], "inputValue": null, "timeTaken": 0, "timeLeftWhenAttempted": null, "status": "notVisited", "_id": "6a4a1f1f9cbf3c651306d0ac", "uid": "6a4a1f1f9cbf3c651306d0ad"}, {"questionId": "69de4f2c2ee0